content.text:
The root cause is the `recommendation` service, which was crash-looping and then left with no available pod. Its failure reached users only through `frontend`'s `/recommendations` endpoint, which returns 500s. Other services' changes (geo CPU, the profile/attractions/user call shifts) did not reach users, so I did not name them.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "recommendation",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, metric, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='recommendation' AND metric='k8s.deployment.available' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Recommendation deployment reports 0 available pods for the whole incident window, versus 1 in normal."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, metric, value, attr_k8s_pod_name FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'recommendation%' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.restarts','k8s.pod.uptime') ORDER BY time", "claim": "Recommendation pod restart counter climbs 8 to 12 during the incident, then its metrics stop after 05:21:15."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='recommendation' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Recommendation emits almost no spans in the incident (1 vs 371 normal), so it is effectively gone."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "recommendation", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) n, avg(duration)/1e6 AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('recommendation.Recommendation/GetRecommendations','HTTP /recommendations') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Frontend's calls to recommendation all error in about 0.015 ms, and HTTP /recommendations returns 500 for 642 requests."}]}
  ]
}
```

